WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
Hey, welcome to Tesla Short's Time, Daily, Episode 481.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.100
It's May 23rd, 2026, and I am Patrick and Vancouver.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.540
Lots happening across deliveries, FSD, and the stock today.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.060
Tesla's new magnet patent cuts rare earth content

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:20.220
below 1% by weight, while keeping the parts structurally intact.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.280
Tesla has patent did a process that machines

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.380
a fraction of a millimeter slit into the magnet block.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.480
The slit stops short of cutting through completely.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.360
This allows a rare earth slurry containing

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.680
turbium to diffuse inward from both the slit and the outer surfaces during vacuum baking.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.060
The unbroken magnet keeps its original dimensions.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.880
It eliminates the need for post-process grinding and fragile glued joints.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.220
The approach reduces heavy rare earth usage to less than 1% of magnet weight.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.640
Now turning to vehicles already running next-generation autonomy hardware.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:01.440
Multiple model-wide vehicles configured for robotaxi duty were photographed in Florida,

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:06.520
carrying updated sensor and compute hardware not present on current customer cars.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.240
The sightings indicate Tesla is already running supervised autonomy fleets on production-like

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:17.800
vehicles ahead of wider deployment. Observers noted differences in camera placement

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.000
and roofline hardware consistent with next-generation hardware revisions.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.240
The activity points to ongoing validation work in a new geographic market.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:32.460
Hardware progress on the ground leads naturally to software behavior on public roads.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:41.420
FSD version 14.3.3 avoided an oncoming wide-turning vehicle with smooth matrix headlight adjustment.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:46.980
The clip also captures the matrix headlights adjusting beam patterns in real time.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.860
Owners note the intervention happened without abrupt inputs.

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:56.180
The update appears to handle edge cases that earlier versions left unaddressed.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:01.280
One driver reported the first actual issue encountered on the new version yet

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.120
was still able to reposition the car and preserve the street counter.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:10.140
The post highlights how rarely problems now surface compared with prior releases.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.360
Community replies focus on the recovery behavior rather than the fault itself.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.340
The tone suggests growing tolerance for occasional interventions.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:25.480
Autonomy software advances coincide with Tesla's physical expansion plans in new markets.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.560
Tesla has expressed interest in opening a dedicated showroom and service facility in Hydubad,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.520
India as part of broader expansion planning.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.220
Local officials confirmed discussions are underway for a physical retail and after-sales presence.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.520
The move would mark Tesla's first formal service footprint in the city

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.220
and follows similar interest expressed in other Indian markets.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:51.960
No timeline or site details have been released yet.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:57.160
Retail growth in India contrasts with shifting priorities at the Beijing Auto Show.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.460
Multiple Chinese automakers use the Beijing Auto Show to showcase

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:07.200
Robotaxi concepts and AI-driven driving systems rather than traditional consumer models.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:13.020
The shift reflects a broader industry focus on autonomy and fleet services as growth

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:19.540
in private eb sales slows. Tesla's own China strategy was referenced in coverage of the event

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.020
as a benchmark competitors are now matching.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:28.380
The emphasis on Robotaxi's signals a change in capital allocation away from individual

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:34.960
vehicle sales. Industry-wide autonomy focus brings us to a simpler price adjustment closer to home.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:41.120
Tesla lowered the price of the Model 3 in Canada by roughly $8,000 while extending

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.240
at zero to 60 miles per hour time by two seconds compared with the prior configuration.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:51.920
The adjustment aligns the Canadian variant more closely with the US rear-wheel drive model.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:56.920
The change broadens entry-level access but trades some acceleration performance.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:01.460
Fires will now weigh the lower price against the reduced performance spec.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:06.920
Pricing moves in one market sit alongside new cooling ideas for future vehicles.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:13.600
Tesla filed a patent describing a glass roof perforated with an array of small holes intended to

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:19.200
improve cabin cooling efficiency. The design allows air to pass through the roof structure while

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:25.220
maintaining structural and weather sealing integrity. The approach targets reduced reliance on

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:31.780
traditional HX systems in hot climates. If implemented the feature would appear on future vehicle

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:37.960
lines rather than current production models. Vehicle-level efficiency ideas connect to larger-scale

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:43.560
energy storage deployments. Meta partnered with Enbridge to deploy a large renewable energy

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:49.480
installation that will incorporate Tesla battery storage systems. The project supports Meta's

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:54.740
data center power needs and marks another commercial use of Tesla energy products outside the

00:04:54.740 --> 00:05:00.160
automotive business. No capacity figures or contract values were disclosed in the announcement.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.420
The deal expands Tesla's Megapack footprint in utility-scale applications.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:11.480
Institutional capital flows in energy contrast with a notable sovereign fund exit.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:15.400
Norway's central bank sold its entire holdings in Tesla,

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:20.020
Rivian, and Lucid during the first quarter, according to regulatory filings.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:25.340
The moves removed the sovereign fund's exposure to the three USEV companies.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:31.800
No public explanation accompanied the filing. The sales occurred alongside broader portfolio

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:38.080
adjustments reported for the period. Battery strategy changes sit next to real-world longevity

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:46.800
evidence. A UK owner of a 245,000-mile Model 3 completed a 1,300-mile week-long trip at an

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:52.720
energy cost lower than half a tank of gasoline would have required. The vehicle continues daily

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:58.620
service despite its high mileage. The report highlights real-world longevity and operating cost

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:04.580
advantages under heavy use. No charging time or reliability issues were noted during the journey.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:11.620
Owner experience in Europe leads to recent sales chart movement there. The Dasha Sundero regained

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:22.700
the top spot in European sales in April, while the Tesla Model Y fell outside the top 10 in the

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:27.000
high-lights renewed strength for lower-priced internal combustion and hybrid models.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:33.540
No specific Model Y volume figures were released. The result underscores continued price

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:39.620
sensitivity in the European market. Sales softness in one region contrasts with an isolated but

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:45.240
attention-grabbing incident. A cyber truck became stuck after its owner drove it into a lake,

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:51.240
leading to an arrest. The incident occurred outside normal operating conditions and drew quick

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:56.860
social media attention. No details on vehicle damage or recovery costs have surfaced yet.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.400
It stands as an isolated case rather than a pattern.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:07.360
Now, one thing worth watching is the Sovereign Fund exit. Norway's Sovereign Wealth Fund sold

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:13.120
its complete positions in Tesla, Rivian, and Lucid during the first quarter. The exits remove

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:19.180
a high-profile institutional holder from all three companies at once. No accompanying statement

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:24.920
explained the timing or rationale. The sales coincide with the period of mixed EV demand signals

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:31.060
across North America and Europe. Taking a step back from today's headlines, the decision by a

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:37.000
major Sovereign Fund to exit its Tesla stake raises a narrower question than valuation debates

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:43.140
usually allow. The filing shows the sales occurred without any disclosed change in Tesla's vehicle

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:49.680
margins or energy deployment volumes during the same quarter. Historical data from other large funds

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:56.600
indicate that sustained quarterly growth above 15% in energy storage deployments has previously

00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:03.420
coincided with re-entry by similar investors within two quarters. Tesla's vertical integration of

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:09.280
battery and power electronics gives it a direct lever on that metric through cell production ramp

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:15.520
and mega-pack utilization rates. If those rates continue to rise while vehicle gross margins

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:21.580
stabilize, the same balance sheet logic that prompted the exit could support re-entry without any

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:27.280
shift in narrative or macro conditions. Tomorrow, we'll be watching for further details on the

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:33.020
Hydobad facility discussions and any regulatory updates tied to the latest FSD version.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:42.460
That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at $426.01, up $8.16, 2%.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:49.020
If you found this useful, a rating or review on Apple podcasts or Spotify really helps new listeners

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:55.460
find this show. You can also find us on X at Tesla Short's Time. I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:09:02.000
Thanks for listening and I'll see you tomorrow. This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice,

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.900
editorial selection, and analysis are my own.
